<title>AUSTRIA: Austria's Danube mostly reopened as rain subsides.</title>
<headline>Austria's Danube mostly reopened as rain subsides.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stretch of Danube river in Austria from the German border town of Passau through to Linz was reopened to shipping early on Monday morning, Austrian river police said.</p>
<p>However, roughly 50 kilometres of the Danube between the Slovak border and the Freudenau lock east of Vienna remained closed, a river police spokesman in Vienna told Reuters.</p>
<p>The stretch is expected to be reopened by the end of Monday.</p>
<p>Danube shipping was suspended in Austria on Sunday as days of torrential rain in central and eastern Europe took their toll.</p>
</text>
